<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Mod id="84dc210e-0bdd-440a-b1cd-a0a886064863" version="1">
  <Properties>
    <Name>(BNW) Leugi's Barbarian Inmersion Enhancements</Name>
    <Teaser>Changes the name of the Barbarians depending on the Era. Also adds Barbarian Great Generals and other bonuses.</Teaser>
    <Description>Changes the name of the Barbarians depending on the Era human player is at. Also adds Barbarian Great Generals and other bonuses depending on the era (optional).

The names and bonuses are:

Ancient/Classical: Barbarian: No bonuses:
Medieval: Brigand: Ignores Terrain Cost and Withdraws
Renassaince: Pirate: May embark and receives naval bonuses.
Industrial/Modern: Rebel: May embark, can capture enemy units to their side and may move after pillaging.
Postmodern/Future: Terrorist: May embark. May move after pillaging and has increased attack against cities.

The names, promotions and the Great General may be disabled through the Leugi_Barbarian_Settings.lua file</Description>
    <Authors>Leugi</Authors>
    <SpecialThanks>Gedemon, JFD</SpecialThanks>
    <HideSetupGame>0</HideSetupGame>
    <AffectsSavedGames>0</AffectsSavedGames>
    <SupportsSinglePlayer>1</SupportsSinglePlayer>
    <SupportsMultiplayer>1</SupportsMultiplayer>
    <SupportsHotSeat>1</SupportsHotSeat>
    <SupportsMac>1</SupportsMac>
    <ReloadAudioSystem>0</ReloadAudioSystem>
    <ReloadLandmarkSystem>0</ReloadLandmarkSystem>
    <ReloadStrategicViewSystem>0</ReloadStrategicViewSystem>
    <ReloadUnitSystem>1</ReloadUnitSystem>
  </Properties>
